    html: |
      <section class="page-hero" style="background-image:url('assets/img/dest-chongqing.png');"><div class="container"><span class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="tours.html">Destinations</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Chongqing</span><h1>Chongqing <span class="zh" style="font-family:var(--font-zh);font-size:0.65em;color:var(--gold);">重庆</span></h1><p>Chongqing is China's mountain city of fog and fire — a neon-lit metropolis stacked on steep hills where the Yangtze and Jialing rivers meet, and the birthplace of fiery hotpot.</p></div></section>
  - label: "Why visit Chongqing?"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/dest-chongqing.png" alt="Chongqing" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">重<br/>庆</div></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Mountain City</span><h2 class="display-h2">Why visit Chongqing?</h2><p>Chongqing is a city that defies gravity — roads loop over rooftops, a monorail flies straight through a residential tower, and Hongya Cave's golden stilted houses glow above the river at night. Add the world's spiciest hotpot, the Daninghe-side Wulong karst wonders, and a famously warm-hearted local character, and you get one of China's most unforgettable urban adventures.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Iconic experiences in Chongqing"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Must-See Sights</span><h2 class="display-h2">Iconic experiences in Chongqing</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Hongya Cave at Night</h3><p>Eleven stories of illuminated stilted buildings stacked on a cliff above the Jialing River — Chongqing's most iconic skyline scene, best enjoyed on an evening river walk.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Liziba Monorail Through a Building</h3><p>Watch the famous light-rail train slide straight through the 8th floor of a residential tower — a one-of-a-kind ride through the vertical city.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Authentic Chongqing Hotpot</h3><p>The birthplace of Chinese hotpot. Brave the nine-grid beef-tallow pot, or go mild — either way it's a dinner show you'll talk about for years.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Wulong Karst Day Trip</h3><p>A UNESCO World Heritage landscape of natural rock bridges, giant sinkholes and the fairy-tale valley of Furong — an easy day trip from the city.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Yangtze River Cableway</h3><p>Glide across the Yangtze in a cable car for sweeping views of the stacked skyline — the classic way to see the "fog capital" from above.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Ciqikou Ancient Town</h3><p>A Ming-dynasty porcelain port of stone lanes, teahouses and chili-lined courtyards perched on the hillside — old Chongqing in a single afternoon.</p></div></div></div></section>
